      "line_end": 17,
      "title": "Return type change breaks both CLI callers",
      "description": "safeGit now returns a GitResult object, but currentBranch calls name.trim() and changedFiles calls out.split() on it. Neither caller was updated in this change. currentBranch catches the TypeError and always returns null, so the CLI always prints not a git repository and exits. changedFiles would throw a TypeError if it were reached. Update currentBranch and changedFiles to read result.stdout and to check result.code. Or keep the old string-returning function next to the new one.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": "lens:return-shape-contract-break",
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "safeGit now returns a GitResult object, but currentBranch calls name.trim() and changedFiles calls out.split() on it. Neither caller was updated in this change.",
